# A declaration nothing calls is not a dependency.
#
# The emitted C carries the prototype `void vela_probe_unreached(int32_t);` and
# no call, so the linker never looks for the symbol: a program may name a C
# function it does not have, and the compiler is not in the business of
# demanding the library.  This is also where a `-> None` result is exercised
# without a real `void` C function, of which the CRT offers none Vela can spell
# exactly (`srand` takes `unsigned int`, `exit` ends the program).
extern c def vela_probe_unreached(x: i32) -> None

def main() -> None {
    print("the declaration is never called")
}
